<http://example.org/sen0414-ch17ch18-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Fresh narrow lineage: SEN0414 Chapters 17 and 18"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.6.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch17ch18-lineage/1.6.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch17ch18_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment "1.6.0 (2026-11-11): Owner decision on the repeated ZIP story. The owner asked, after the drafts were sent, whether repetition of a story across chapters is controlled; it is not (no deck check, register or shape compares stories across chapters). The chapter 17 ZIP story repeats chapter 11's; the owner decided: replace it with a different story. A new draft file DRAFT_ch17_v1_0_1.md carries the replacement (the 15 February 2008 release of the .doc binary specification); v1_0_0 is kept unchanged. A handover proposing a repeat-control rule was deposited in CME's pending inbox."@en .

ex:ST7_DraftCh17 backlog:hasAuditNote "Revised 2026-11-11 on the owner's decision: 03-materials/ch17/DRAFT_ch17_v1_0_1.md replaces story 2 (ZIP 1989, already told in the chapter 11 story script) with the 2008 .doc specification story, sources Microsoft's Office-blog post and the Library of Congress format pages, with a python-docx check run 2026-11-11 (PackageNotFoundError on an OLE-signature file). The approval gate refers to v1_0_1 for chapter 17 and v1_0_0 for chapter 18." .
